  "description": "## Completed PetWorld workspace\nPersistent shell for the completed workspace.home, workspace.pets, workspace.pet-detail and workspace.countries children. The home page declares parentPageName workspace and renders at /app/home. Use the top-level workspace state as the app default entry: exact workspace arrivals redirect to workspace.home with $state.go('workspace.home', {}, { location: 'replace' }), replacing the parent entry in browser history.\n\nA dedicated lifecycle method installs an exact-parent success hook and one deferred initial check. Angular $timeout defers navigation until after the current transition/digest; registration, current-state and active-transition checks protect child deep links and concurrent navigation. A shared queued/in-flight guard deduplicates initialization and success-hook work. Rejections are handled without automatic retries or redirect loops; the existing overview link remains available. Hooks and pending timers are cleaned up after successful workspace exit. syncNavigation only computes menu state and never initiates transitions.\n\nCore Navigation, declarative links, child-pages outlet, responsive collapse, theme hooks, keyboard focus behavior, viewport minimum sizing and Petstore v2/Countries GraphQL references are preserved. Media-query and focus listeners are removed after successful workspace exit.",
  "name": "workspace",
  "params": {},
  "type": "page",
  "url": "/app",
  "variables": [
    {
      "name": "$state",
      "type": "service"
    },
    {
      "name": "$transitions",
      "type": "service"
    },
    {
      "name": "$window",
      "type": "service"
    },
    {
      "name": "$rootScope",
      "type": "service"
    },
    {
      "name": "$timeout",
      "type": "service"
    },
    {
      "description": "Native Navigation collapse state; initialized from a small-screen media query and subsequently controlled by its built-in toggle.",
      "name": "navCollapsed",
      "type": "property",
      "value": "false"
    },
    {
      "description": "Declarative links to the completed workspace sections, with a defensive registration-time URL fallback.",
      "name": "navItems",
      "type": "property",
      "value": "[]"
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows the existing parent welcome fallback only while exact workspace is active, before its landing redirect completes or if it fails.",
      "name": "isShellOnly",
      "type": "property",
      "value": "true"
    },
    {
      "body": "const main = $ctrl.$window.document.getElementById('petworld-workspace-content');\nif (main) {\n  main.focus({ preventScroll: true });\n}",
      "description": "Moves keyboard focus to the semantic main landmark without changing route or forcing scroll.",
      "invokeOnLoad": false,
      "isAsync": false,
      "name": "focusContent",
      "parameters": [],
      "returnType": {
        "name": "any"
      },
      "type": "method",
      "watch": []
    },
    {
      "body": "const current = $ctrl.$state.current.name || '';\n$ctrl.isShellOnly = current === 'workspace';\nconst sections = [\n  { label: 'Overview', state: 'workspace.home', path: '#!/app/home' },\n  { label: 'Pet catalogue', state: 'workspace.pets', path: '#!/app/pets' },\n  { label: 'Countries', state: 'workspace.countries', path: '#!/app/countries' }\n];\n// Defensive URL fallback during route registration; all section children are implemented.\nconst links = sections.map((section) => {\n  const active = current === section.state || current.startsWith(section.state + '.') || (section.state === 'workspace.pets' && (current === 'workspace.pet-detail' || current.startsWith('workspace.pet-detail.')));\n  return {\n    label: section.label,\n    evaluateLabel: false,\n    onClick: 'link',\n    openIn: 'current-window',\n    link: $ctrl.$state.get(section.state) ? { type: 'state', state: section.state, parameters: {} } : { type: 'url', path: section.path, evaluate: false },\n    checkedWhen: active ? 'true' : 'false'\n  };\n});\n$ctrl.navItems = [{ label: 'WORKSPACE', evaluateLabel: false, menuItems: links }];",
      "description": "Computes active-section checks, grouping pet-detail under Pet catalogue. Registration guards protect declarative menu links. No routing side effects occur in this watched method.",
      "invokeOnLoad": true,
      "isAsync": false,
      "name": "syncNavigation",
      "parameters": [],
      "returnType": {
        "name": "any"
      },
      "type": "method",
      "watch": [
        "$ctrl.$state.current.name"
      ]
    },
    {
      "body": "const media = $ctrl.$window.matchMedia('(max-width: 767px)');\nlet disposed = false;\n$ctrl.navCollapsed = media.matches;\nconst onResize = () => {\n  $ctrl.$rootScope.$evalAsync(() => {\n    if (!disposed) { $ctrl.navCollapsed = media.matches; }\n  });\n};\nif (media.addEventListener) {\n  media.addEventListener('change', onResize);\n} else {\n  media.addListener(onResize);\n}\nconst unsubscribe = $ctrl.$transitions.onSuccess({ to: 'workspace.**' }, () => {\n  $ctrl.$rootScope.$evalAsync(() => {\n    if (disposed) { return; }\n    $ctrl.syncNavigation();\n    if (media.matches) { $ctrl.navCollapsed = true; }\n    $ctrl.focusContent();\n  });\n});\n// A successful exit tears down this shell's external listeners.\nconst unsubscribeExit = $ctrl.$transitions.onSuccess({ from: 'workspace.**' }, (transition) => {\n  const destination = transition.to().name;\n  if (destination === 'workspace' || destination.startsWith('workspace.')) { return; }\n  disposed = true;\n  unsubscribe();\n  unsubscribeExit();\n  if (media.removeEventListener) {\n    media.removeEventListener('change', onResize);\n  } else {\n    media.removeListener(onResize);\n  }\n});",
      "description": "Uses injected $rootScope for digest-safe responsive updates and successful transition hooks for focus and listener cleanup, without relying on $ctrl.$scope. Cleanup runs only after leaving the workspace successfully, so canceled transitions retain menu behavior.",
      "invokeOnLoad": true,
      "isAsync": false,
      "name": "initializeShell",
      "parameters": [],
      "returnType": {
        "name": "any"
      },
      "type": "method",
      "watch": []
    },
    {
      "body": "let disposed = false;\nlet queued = null;\nlet redirecting = false;\nconst scheduleRedirect = () => {\n  if (disposed || queued || redirecting) { return; }\n  // Defer beyond route setup and the parent success hook; never navigate from a digest watch.\n  queued = $ctrl.$timeout(() => {\n    queued = null;\n    if (disposed || redirecting || $ctrl.$state.current.name !== 'workspace') { return; }\n    // Do not supersede any initial or user-requested child transition. Its parent success hook can schedule again.\n    if ($ctrl.$state.transition || !$ctrl.$state.get('workspace.home')) { return; }\n    redirecting = true;\n    try {\n      const navigation = $ctrl.$state.go('workspace.home', {}, { location: 'replace' });\n      navigation.catch(error => {\n        // Superseded/aborted transitions are expected when the user navigates elsewhere.\n        if (!disposed && error && error.type !== 2 && error.type !== 3 && error.type !== 5) {\n          $ctrl.$window.console.error('PetWorld overview redirect failed.', error);\n        }\n      }).finally(() => {\n        redirecting = false;\n      });\n    } catch (error) {\n      redirecting = false;\n      $ctrl.$window.console.error('PetWorld overview redirect failed.', error);\n    }\n  }, 0);\n  // Cancellation on successful exit is intentional, not an unhandled rejection.\n  queued.catch(() => {});\n};\nconst unsubscribeParent = $ctrl.$transitions.onSuccess({ to: 'workspace' }, () => {\n  scheduleRedirect();\n});\nconst unsubscribeExit = $ctrl.$transitions.onSuccess({ from: 'workspace.**' }, transition => {\n  const destination = transition.to().name;\n  if (destination === 'workspace' || destination.startsWith('workspace.')) { return; }\n  disposed = true;\n  unsubscribeParent();\n  unsubscribeExit();\n  if (queued) {\n    $ctrl.$timeout.cancel(queued);\n    queued = null;\n  }\n});\n// Covers initialization after the initial success event; shares the same queue with onSuccess.\nscheduleRedirect();",
      "description": "Lifecycle-only exact-parent redirect, independent of watched menu computation. One deferred check plus an exact workspace success hook share queued/in-flight guards. Rechecks state, route registration and active transition immediately before normal $state.go with location replace. Successful exits dispose hooks and cancel deferred work; redirect rejections are reported without retry loops.",
      "invokeOnLoad": true,
      "isAsync": false,
      "name": "initializeLandingRedirect",
      "parameters": [],
      "returnType": {
        "name": "any"
      },
      "type": "method",
      "watch": []
    }
  ]
}
